isosceles times (no kernel involved): 12 per period

  kernel                    crossings   max |t - t_isosceles|
  --------------------------------------------------------------
  Gaussian  sigma=0.30             12   9.37e-13
  Gaussian  sigma=0.60             12   5.41e-14
  exponential exp(-2r)             12   2.15e-14
  inverse   1/(1+r^2)              12   1.08e-14
  Epanechnikov-like                12   5.77e-15
  heavy tail 1/(1+r)               12   6.66e-15

The wall locus does not depend on the kernel, only on whether the kernel
is monotone. The bandwidth cannot move a wall; it can only decide whether
the crowding difference is large enough to be resolved numerically.
